{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Moses said to Joshua</b> — From here it appears that from the day he came before him, Moses called him Joshua, as it is written (Exodus 32:17): \"And Joshua heard the voice of the people.\" And the verse that is stated in the matter of the spies: \"And Moses called Hoshea bin Nun Joshua\" (Numbers 13:16) — it speaks of him first, to inform us that this Hoshea bin Nun, whom he chose among the spies, is the one whom Moses called Joshua. And according to the words of our Sages (Sotah 34b), who said: \"May YHWH save you from the counsel of the spies,\" it is to tell that on account of this matter — for Moses knew that he was going to go with the spies — he called him this name. Or we may say that then Moses fixed this name for him before the assembly, so that his name would no longer be called Hoshea, but his name would be Joshua.\n\nThe reason that Moses commanded Joshua to wage battle against Amalek is so that he [Moses] would pray with the lifting of hands on the top of the hill, and he went up there so that he would see Israel fighting and set his eye upon them for good, and also they would see him spreading his hands heavenward and increasing in prayer, and they would trust in him and add strength and might.\n\nAnd in Pirkei d'Rabbi Eliezer (chapter 44) further: all Israel went out from their tents and saw Moses kneeling on his knees, and they kneeling on their knees; his face falling to the ground, and they falling on their faces to the ground; spreading his hands to the heavens, and they spreading their hands to the heavens — just as the prayer leader prays, so all the people answer after him. And the Holy One, blessed be He, brought down Amalek and his people by the hand of Joshua. And if so, the meaning of \"and the staff of Elohim in my hand\" is to say that when he went up on the top of the hill and saw Amalek, he extended his hand with the staff to bring upon them plagues of pestilence and sword and destruction — as in the matter stated regarding Joshua: \"Extend the javelin that is in your hand toward Ai, for into your hand I will give it\" (Joshua 8:18) — for at the time he was praying with his hands spread to the heavens, he would hold nothing in his hand.\n\nAnd the entire matter that Moses our teacher did was because Amalek was a mighty and very powerful nation, and Israel were not trained in warfare and had never seen it, as He said: \"Lest the people reconsider when they see war\" (Exodus 13:17), and they [Israel] were faint and exhausted, as written in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 25:18). Therefore he feared them and needed all this prayer and supplication.\n\nAnd it is possible that Moses feared lest he [Amalek] prevail by his sword, because he is a nation that inherits the sword from the blessing of the elder [Isaac], who said to him: \"And by your sword you shall live\" (Genesis 27:40), for the war from this family is the first and the last for Israel, for Amalek is of the seed of Esau (ibid. 36:12), and from him came the war against us at the beginning of the nations, and from the seed of Esau came the exile and the final destruction to us, as our Sages say (Avodah Zarah 2b) that today we are in the exile of Edom. And when he is defeated, and he and the many peoples that are with him are weakened, from there we shall be saved forever, as it says (Obadiah 1:21): \"And saviors shall ascend Mount Zion to judge the mountain of Esau, and the kingdom shall be YHWH's.\" And behold, all that Moses and Joshua did with them at the first, Elijah and Mashiach ben Yosef shall do with their seed; therefore Moses strove mightily in this matter."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The citation 'ובמשנה תורה (דברים כה יח)' refers to the book of Deuteronomy; the phrase 'ויתכן שפחד משה פן יתגבר בחרבו' — the subject of 'יתגבר' (prevail) is Amalek, and 'בחרבו' refers to Amalek's sword, as clarified by the immediately following explanation about the blessing of the sword given to Esau."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:02.105412284Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}